meta {
  name: Plans - List
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/plans
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const plans = res.body.data?.plans;
    if (Array.isArray(plans) && plans.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("planId", plans[0].id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Lists the active plans for the workspace. Requires the `billing.view`
  permission.

  Each plan carries a price for all four billing windows
  (`price_monthly`, `price_quarterly`, `price_yearly`, `price_lifetime`)
  plus `available_intervals` — the subset actually on sale right now.
  Offer only those; anything else 422s at checkout.

  An interval can be priced but withdrawn, so do not infer the buy options
  from which `price_*` fields are non-zero. An interval is absent from
  `available_intervals` when the plan is inactive, when it is switched off
  estate-wide (`config('billing.intervals')`), when the plan's own
  `enabled_intervals` excludes it, or when no Stripe price is set.

  Stores the first plan's ID in the `planId` collection variable so
  `Billing/Subscription - Checkout` works without hand-editing.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { plans } }`.
}
